{
  "_notes": [
    "age_terms: words that mean a child, an age group or a size or height standing in for age, in English, Hindi in Latin script and Devanagari; any of them makes a request a cannot. Text is NFC normalised before matching.",
    "boy and girl usually mean a child, so they count. Job titles that use them for adults (delivery boy, office boy) are in not_age_phrases and never count.",
    "A zone or line name with an age word in it is a place only when the age word sits directly before place words and nothing else is in the name (kids play area, toddler pool, girls toilet, children's park). Otherwise it is refused (it says who, not where). Only such names are masked before the check.",
    "age_patterns catch explicit age forms only: N or a number word before year, yr, yrs or yo (7-year-old, seven year-old, a ten yr old, 8 yrs, 7yo), aged N, N years of age, under N years, under-12s and u18, a person of about N, N saal ka, class 5 student and 5th grader, and heights (shorter than 4 feet, under 120 cm, 3 ft tall). Counts (a group of 5, a crowd of 20, a stay of 2 days) and durations (kept for 7 years, under 5 minutes) are not ages.",
    "student alone is allowed, since college students are adults; school student, school uniform, class 5 student and the like count.",
    "child_anchors and ordinary_anchors drive the meaning check (agent/meaning.py): a looks_like or zone_looks_like text is refused when the image model's text tower puts it nearer its nearest child anchor than its nearest ordinary anchor by Tuning signals.child_meaning_margin. The calibration is in backend/tests/test_privacy_fix.py."
  ],
